      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> Singleton Bean is eagerly created .\n\n-> Whereas prototype bean is lazily created . --> $1BeanScope-Ex-02\n\n-> But if prototype bean is set as dependency inside a singleton\nbean  it is also eagrly created when the container start ..\n --> $1BeanScope-Ex-03\n\n-> Spring first resolve constructor-arg before calling constructor .\n\n-> Singleton scope bean should be used for staeless beans .\n\n-> Prototype scope is used for all beans that are stateful beans .\n\n-> stateless bean refers to a bean that does not maintain any\ninternal state between method calls .\n\n-> Means instance is either has no property/instance variable or if it\nhas property than it is not changing for multiple objects .\n\n\nWhy spring bean is singleton by default \n------------------------------------------------\n\n-> To avaoid OutOfMemoryError and save memory .\n\n-> When a bean is singleton, only one shared instance of bean will be\nmanaged and all requests for that bean result in that one specific\nbean instance being returned .\n\n\n-> If we want instance to be singleton but intialized lazily than we\ncan use attribute lazy-init=\"true\"   --> $4BeanScope-Ex-04",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> Singleton Bean is eagerly created .\n\n-> Whereas prototype bean is lazily created . --> $1BeanScope-Ex-02\n\n-> But if prototype bean is set as dependency inside a singleton bean  it is also eagrly created when the container start ..\n --> $1BeanScope-Ex-03\n\n-> Spring first resolve constructor-arg before calling constructor .\n\n-> Singleton scope bean should be used for staeless beans .\n\n-> Prototype scope is used for all beans that are stateful beans .\n\n-> stateless bean refers to a bean that does not maintain any internal state between method calls .\n\n-> Means instance is either has no property/instance variable or if it has property than it is not changing for multiple objects .\n\n\nWhy spring bean is singleton by default \n------------------------------------------------\n\n-> To avaoid OutOfMemoryError and save memory .\n\n-> When a bean is singleton, only one shared instance of bean will be managed and all requests for that bean result in that one specific bean instance being returned .\n\n\n-> If we want instance to be singleton but intialized lazily than we can use attribute lazy-init=\"true\"   --> $4BeanScope-Ex-04",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
